{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund a museum dedicated to the Victoria Cross recipients",
        "additional_details": "The stories of Victoria Cross recipients are currently spread across regimental museums, memorials, cemeteries, private collections and locations around the world. There is no single dedicated place where we can remember these heroes and learn their stories. A National Victoria Cross Museum would provide a permanent home to commemorate every recipient, bringing their stories together and ensuring their extraordinary courage and sacrifice are preserved for future generations.",
        "background": "Fund a dedicated National Victoria Cross Museum to preserve and share the stories of those awarded Britain\u2019s highest decoration for valour. It would honour their courage and sacrifice, educate future generations and provide these remarkable stories with a permanent national home.",
